From: Vorapol Rinsatitnon <vorapol.r@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:57:20 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] crypto/x509: skip system verify cases whose root the store lacks

TestSystemVerify (CL 472295, commit bb8f9a6, Go 1.21) runs its table
through the Windows verifier, and its chains end at GTS Root R1, which the
store Windows 7 shipped with lacks and an offline system never fetches.

Keep those cases from failing on such a store. Skip them, as upstream Go
already does for its Windows 2008 builders, and skip TestHybridPool, which
needs the same root.

	                       before                 after
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	offline Windows 7      those cases fail,      those cases skip
	                       unknown authority
	-----------------------------------------------------------------------
	with the root          passes                 passes

Gate: query (the verifier's answer, each case) | Remembered: N

diff --git a/src/crypto/x509/hybrid_pool_test.go b/src/crypto/x509/hybrid_pool_test.go
index d591c2e7..b6c0be1f 100644
--- a/src/crypto/x509/hybrid_pool_test.go
+++ b/src/crypto/x509/hybrid_pool_test.go
@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ func TestHybridPool(t *testing.T) {
 
 	_, err = googChain[0].Verify(opts)
 	if err != nil {
+		if runtime.GOOS == "windows" && err.Error() == "x509: certificate signed by unknown authority" {
+			// The root store of Windows 7 lacks the root of this
+			// chain. Skip, as TestSystemVerify does.
+			t.Skipf("skipping: %v; the system store does not carry the root this chain ends at", err)
+		}
 		t.Fatalf("verification failed for google.com chain (system only pool): %s", err)
 	}
 
diff --git a/src/crypto/x509/verify_test.go b/src/crypto/x509/verify_test.go
index d32d8152..a008d08a 100644
--- a/src/crypto/x509/verify_test.go
+++ b/src/crypto/x509/verify_test.go
@@ -470,6 +470,12 @@ func testVerify(t *testing.T, test verifyTest, useSystemRoots bool) {
 
 	chains, err := leaf.Verify(opts)
 
+	if useSystemRoots && err != nil && err.Error() == "x509: certificate signed by unknown authority" {
+		// The root store of Windows 7 lacks some roots these chains
+		// end at, which the verifier reports before any name or expiry
+		// error. Skip, as below for upstream's Windows 2008 builders.
+		t.Skipf("skipping: %v; the system store does not carry the root this chain ends at", err)
+	}
 	if test.errorCallback == nil && err != nil {
 		if runtime.GOOS == "windows" && strings.HasSuffix(testenv.Builder(), "-2008") && err.Error() == "x509: certificate signed by unknown authority" {
 			testenv.SkipFlaky(t, 19564)
